    {
      "id": "5rXS6Q8lQfSCML-rNDLLr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -869.5109015196449,
      "y": 43.20926264224494,
      "width": 307.2998046875,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 133942255,
      "version": 386,
      "versionNonce": 1630449697,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789856125928,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "My understood about it (pt-br)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "My understood about it (pt-br)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "42DLiENSw2At-P9xN-yjF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 218.26427266937935,
      "y": 92.80166427679245,
      "width": 900.1546962321925,
      "height": 111.83503431673623,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 706665519,
      "version": 1629,
      "versionNonce": 302223439,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789856680503,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Classes should not be forced to depend on methods they do not use!\n\nThis principle prevents bloated interfaces—interfaces containing many methods that aren't actually needed by the client, the final class, or every implementing class.\n\nWhen bloated interfaces are implemented, classes are forced to implement methods they don't use; this often results in empty methods sitting in the code doing\nnothing, simply because the class was required to implement them.\n\nUltimately, remember: no class should be forced to depend on or implement methods it will not use!",
      "fontSize": 11.183503431673623,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Classes should not be forced to depend on methods they do not use!\n\nThis principle prevents bloated interfaces—interfaces containing many methods that aren't actually needed by the client, the final class, or every implementing class.\n\nWhen bloated interfaces are implemented, classes are forced to implement methods they don't use; this often results in empty methods sitting in the code doing nothing, simply because the class was required to implement them.\n\nUltimately, remember: no class should be forced to depend on or implement methods it will not use!",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
